Z||000000||yo_sweet||12-23-2001||12:35 AM||||what's the best way to do this without breaking them?<P>------------------<BR>1986 Fiero SE 2.8lv6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dance.gif">  <P><BR>www.geocities.com/acme_s2000/intro.html<BR>yo_sweet!||||reg||1
Z||000001||edbone||12-23-2001||01:04 AM||||I use a hook pick tool and pry on each corner only,never had a problem.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/edbonesig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Smoooooth GT||12-23-2001||01:45 AM||||They just 'pop' off...  eeezz...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">                       <BR>      <P><A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A>   <BR>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<BR>"Smoooooth GT"<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||6
Z||000003||JohnF||12-23-2001||08:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by edbone:<BR><B>I use a hook pick tool and pry on each corner only,never had a problem.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>A thin, flat-bladed screwdriver used to pry up each corner works great, also.  Just put padding under the shaft of the screwdriver to insure the dash is not harmed when prying.  <P>BTW - speaker covers can be recoved by buying as little as 1/8 yd of professional grade speaker grille material from almost any fabric shop (costs about a buck).  Radio Shack won't sell less than a yd or so (and they are expensive).<P>||||reg||12
Z||000004||LZeitgeist||12-23-2001||10:00 AM||||I made my own hook by bending the last 1/8" of a straightened paper clip into a 90-degree angle.<P>Slip hooked end between dash and edge of speaker cover, turn 90-degrees and gently lift straight up until the corner pin pops free from the rubber mounting grommet.<P>I would not suggest prying the covers up with a screwdriver, as the dashes in our cars are very old, and even the gentlest prying may leave a dent in the edge of the speaker opening... one that will visually vex you, being in plain sight, for the rest of the time you own the car... trust me, I know this from my previous coupe. (I wish I had thought of the paperclip in the first place...)||||reg||1
